  "frozen_placement": "Same frozen A sheets, result tokens, cache construction, positions and boundaries as recon12. All twelve result lines stay in every message. B keeps the same private facts. Only the requested output changes to one label for one named carrier. Greedy decoding with a fixed short allowance. Each question starts from an independent copy of its message cache.",
  "stats_note": "Bootstrap resamples the nine source cases (2000 draws). The 108 labels per condition are not independent examples; nine clusters give wide intervals. Deltas are right minus left. cases_increased / cases_decreased count the direction of the change in that metric; for error counts an increase is worse.",
  "interpretation_guide": "If transferred R becomes accurate when queried one carrier at a time, the states can support correct answers under a targeted request; investigate carrier-label association and errors accumulating over the longer response. That would justify examining receiver attention, not prove attention is the sole cause. If transferred R stays poor while fresh R stays strong, the reuse problem persists under a focused request; proceed to matched K/V replacement and attention diagnostics with fresh R under the identical support as the reference. If fresh R and text also deteriorate, first inspect the single-label prompt and scoring; that would not isolate cache reuse. Reconstruction is a diagnostic reference here, not an efficient repair, and the processing totals are not a transmission or speed claim."
